 6117: def default_start_agent_here(project_root: Path) -> str:
 6118:     assignment_path = locate_flow_root(project_root) / "assignments" / "first-assignment.yaml"
 6119:     assignment_rel = rel(assignment_path, project_root) if assignment_path.is_file() else ".pf/assignments/"
 6120:     run_block = start_agent_run_block(project_root)
 6121:     return f"""# Start Agent Here
 6122: 
 6123: You are working inside a ProcessForge-enabled project.
 6124: 
 6125: ## Preferred Path
 6126: 
 6127: 1. Read `.pf/AGENTS.md`.
 6128: 2. Call `pf.context` with this project root; use the current snapshot only as a
 6129:    file-only fallback when MCP is unavailable.
 6130: 3. Use `pf.search` and `pf.resolve` for project-authorized resources.
 6131: 4. Perform local read-only analysis.
 6132: 5. Call `pf.work.start` with the high-level objective when work becomes
 6133:    substantive, then follow the selected assignment and capsule.
 6134: 6. Use ProcessForge artifacts, reviews, logs, and handoffs for durable outputs.
 6135: 
 6136: ## Infrastructure Boundary
 6137: 
 6138: During ordinary project work, do not install, start, restart, or repair PF
 6139: Runtime, MCP, host hooks, or Agent Ledger. Report an operator-level blocker if
 6140: Forge infrastructure is required but unavailable. Garage work does not require
 6141: Runtime, hooks, or a manually created Ledger session.
 6142: 
 6143: Do not expose local absolute paths from `.pf/process-forge.local.yaml`. Do not
 6144: call a distribution-local CLI path from this project root unless this project
 6145: is the ProcessForge distribution itself.
 6146: 
 6147: ## Current Assignment
 6148: 
 6149: - File: `{assignment_rel}`
 6150: - Goal: Verify this project is ready for ProcessForge assignment work.
 6151: 
 6152: {run_block}
 6153: """
 6154: 
