docs/concepts/processforge-events.md:3:This compatibility page points to the current event model:
docs/concepts/processforge-events.md:5:- [Process Events](process-events.md) documents derived project events.
docs/concepts/processforge-events.md:6:- [Hooks And Events](hooks-events.md) documents native raw ingress, provider adapters, conversation capture and replay boundaries.
docs/concepts/processforge-events.md:8:Do not treat `.pf/runtime/events/events.ndjson` as the complete journal of native hook activity. Raw native events remain private workplace records.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:3:ProcessForge separates native agent observations from ProcessForge events and from project-visible chat records.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:6:native agent hook/event
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:8:  -> workplace private raw ingress
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:10:  -> project event, conversation record, Ledger effect, or no derived effect
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:15:- A **raw native event** is the provider payload. The Raw Event Journal is private, workplace-scoped storage at `<workplace>/runtime/agent-events/`.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:16:- A **normalized PF event** is a provider-neutral derived fact.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:17:- A **project event** is a private project record in `.pf/runtime/events/events.ndjson`; it is not the complete hook journal.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:18:- A **chat message** is a private transcript record. Its accompanying `chat.message.recorded` event is metadata-only by default.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:19:- A **delivery attempt** is outbox work. An **operator log** is a separate process artifact, not an event substitute.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:25:`tools/pf_runtime/codex_hooks.py` is a thin adapter. Its normalized mappings include session lifecycle, compaction and tool facts. Every registered event is accepted raw-first. `UserPromptSubmit` records the user prompt, `Stop` records `last_assistant_message`, and `SubagentStop` records the subagent final message when their Ledger session and project binding are valid.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:27:This capability is not proof that every Codex hook is registered in an environment. The distribution does not install a host `.codex/hooks.json`. Adapter acceptance, normalized mapping, conversation mapping and actual host registration are separate facts. Unknown native events can remain raw-only.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:29:Generic interactive Codex assistant responses and host subagent responses are captured only where Codex provides `last_assistant_message`; interim streaming output and unavailable provider fields remain raw-only or absent.
docs/concepts/hooks-events.md:33:the hooks; inspect `/hooks` in the target Codex client. See
